{#
  "Show password" control for one or more password boxes (#29). `controls` is the space-separated
  ids of the boxes it shows and hides. It is hidden here and revealed by portal.js, so without
  JavaScript there is no control and the boxes simply stay hidden. It has no name, so it is never
  submitted, and it leaves each box's autocomplete alone for password managers. Its words change
  ("Show password" / "Hide password") to say what it does next; it has no aria-pressed (D133,
  as GOV.UK does it).
#}
{% macro password_toggle(controls, text) -%}
<button
  class="link-action password-toggle"
  type="button"
  data-password-toggle
  aria-controls="{{ controls }}"
  data-show-label="{{ text.show_password }}"
  data-hide-label="{{ text.hide_password }}"
  hidden
>{{ text.show_password }}</button>
{%- endmacro %}
